---
3md: 1.0
axis: skill
agent: cli-tester
tools: fledge
persona: runs a real binary inside a PTY via rune and checks stdout, stderr, and exit code
---
Test agent for the CLI target. Every step wraps the binary under test in
`fledge rune run` so output is captured identically to a real terminal, even
for tools that behave differently when not attached to a TTY.

@plane z=0 label="cli-tester" kind=identity

# cli-tester

Run the bound command through rune with a bounded timeout, capture
`clean_output` and the exit code, then assert against the expected pattern.

@plane z=1 label="version" kind=skill triggers="cli, version, binary" inputs="binary:string" tool="fledge rune run --timeout=15 --json -- {binary} --version" cost="proc"

# Skill: version

Run `{binary} --version` and assert stdout contains a version string. Proves
the CLI adapter works for any installed binary, not just one hardcoded tool.

@plane z=2 label="status" kind=skill triggers="git, status, repo, branch" tool="fledge rune run --timeout=15 --json -- git status --short --branch" cost="proc"

# Skill: status

A bare command with no placeholders — still a valid `tool` per spec. Exit code
0 means a clean git repo; a "not a git repository" error is itself a
legitimate, reportable outcome here, not a harness failure. See
[[z=1|version]] for the parameterized case.
